        },
        {
          "id": "step-1.2",
          "claim": "Put $u=|p|^2/(m^2c^2)\\ge0$ and $h(u)=1-(1+u)^{-1/2}$. By [F2], $h(0)=0$ and $h'(s)=\\frac12(1+s)^{-3/2}\\le\\frac12$ for $s\\ge0$; if $u>0$, the mean value theorem gives $0\\le h(u)\\le u/2$, and for $u=0$ the same holds by equality. Hence, for every $(x,p)\\in K$, $|V_c(p)-p/m|=(|p|/m)h(u)\\le P_{\\max}^3/(2m^3c^2)$. Expanding the component definition in [F3] gives $|a\\times b|^2=|a|^2|b|^2-(a\\cdot b)^2\\le|a|^2|b|^2$, so $\\|G_c(t,x,p)-G_N(t,x,p)\\|_* = |V_c-p/m|/L_*+|q|\\,|(V_c-p/m)\\times\\mathbf B(t,x)|/P_*\\le\\frac{P_{\\max}^3}{2m^3c^2}\\left(\\frac1{L_*}+\\frac{|q|B_{\\max}}{P_*}\\right)=C_*\\epsilon_c$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "L2",
