        {
          "id": "step-3.1",
          "claim": "The trajectories have the same initial state, are solutions on $[0,T]$, and stay in the compact convex set $K$. Apply [L3] with initial discrepancy zero, comparison-field Lipschitz constant $L$, and field error $\\eta=C_*\\epsilon_c$ from step 1.2. It gives $\\|z_c(t)-z_N(t)\\|_*\\le C_*\\epsilon_c t e^{Lt}\\le C_*\\epsilon_c T e^{LT}$ for every $t\\in[0,T]$. Since $\\epsilon_c=c_*^2/c^2$ and the other constants are fixed, the finite-interval error is $O(c^{-2})$.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "step 1.2",
            "step 2.1",
            "L3",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-4.1",
          "claim": "The inversion formula and $|p_c|\\le P_{\\max}$ imply $|\\dot x_c|=|V_c(p_c)|\\le P_{\\max}/m$ and hence $|\\dot x_c|/c\\le P_{\\max}/(mc)\\le\\delta$. Apply [L4] pointwise to the worldline speed $\\dot x_c$ to obtain the two stated kinetic remainders. This only adds kinematic estimates; it does not derive a trajectory comparison from them.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "step 1.1",
            "L2",
            "L4",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
